# Error fix classes (recurring bugs)

Before patching a playtest issue that looks familiar, read `docs/research/ERROR-FIX-LOG.md` and map it to a **failure class**.

| Class | Owner |
|---|---|
| A Turn / proxy | `classifyTurnFailure` + `gmProxy` + refund/restore in `useGame` |
| B Opening contract | `openingEstablishment` / alone covers / OpeningContract |
| C Quest coherence | `questPlay` + `applyErrorRepairs` |
| D Continuity prose | `runWarden` + `proseWarden` |
| E Chrome / HUD | `Hud.tsx` layout (viewport), not stamp-only |
| F Hosted art | `generate-image` + memorable policy |
| G Save schema | `saveMigration.applySaveRepair` |
| H Deploy / ops | stamp + edge redeploy checklist |

**Code:** `src/game/errorRepairWarden.ts` — deterministic auto-repair on load/Continue; turn-fail classification for player toasts.

**Do not** invent a new Continuity-Warden LLM path for these — Continuity Warden is classifier-only (see research spec). Prefer extending `applyErrorRepairs` / OpeningContract / HUD layout.

Open playtest tickets still wait for John to call the next update batch unless he asks to ship now.
